y." :question/worked-solution "Remember that an augmented matrix is in row echelon form if its coefficient matrix satisfies the following conditions:\n\n- All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the bottom of the matrix.\n- Each leading entry of a row is in a column to the right of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied). \n\n$$\nA=\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}6 & 0 & 0 & 8 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1 & 5\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nB=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}8 & 7 & 5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 9\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ is not in row echelon form since ${c}_{21}\\ne 0$ (condition  II is violated).\n\n$$\nC=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}0 & 1 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 5\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $A$ and $B$ are in row echelon form."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186341838 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "60637292-3e09-530b-ac61-fcbbce897d41" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467962} {:answer/id #uuid "e4dad7c2-9a72-5985-95d5-14eb19840971" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467963}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186467962} :answer-field/id #uuid "bf03a675-2bed-5618-b8f1-977c4c5732ba" :answer-field/key "A" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468702} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8421492d-9fc4-581e-9662-4c6ad1d30585" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467964} {:answer/id #uuid "57892105-0d46-58cf-b489-d7654d7df5df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467965}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186467965} :answer-field/id #uuid "ac1b36ea-8d6f-51c9-bc43-9c783cb2e595" :answer-field/key "B" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468703} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "75ae5575-30a3-527c-957b-e31d7bd513e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467966} {:answer/id #uuid "a5c77217-c4e4-5860-8c50-aec83eb153e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467967}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186467966} :answer-field/id #uuid "0477e48c-0ee5-5ea3-a796-a287db3e0107" :answer-field/key "C" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468704}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "2d3c090e-cc4f-51d5-a663-f597f7113489" :question/math-academy-id "q-72576" :question/problem "Which of the following augmented matrices are in row echelon form?\n\n$$\nA=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}2 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2\\end{array}\\right],\\,B=\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}1 & 0 & -2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 5\\end{array}\\right],\\,C=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}2 & 0 & 5 & 8 \\\\ 1 & -4 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 4\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that an augmented matrix is in row echelon form if its coefficient matrix satisfies the following conditions:\n\n- All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the bottom of the matrix.\n- Each leading entry of a row is in a column to the right of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is not in row echelon form since the second row contains only zeros and it is not at the bottom of the matrix (condition I is violated).\n\n$$\nA=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}2 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nB=\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}1 & 0 & -2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 5\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ is not in row echelon form since ${c}_{21}\\ne 0$ (condition II is violated).\n\n$$\nC=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}2 & 0 & 5 & 8 \\\\ 1 & -4 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 4\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $B$ is in row echelon form."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186400436 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c63daf6f-eed4-503b-a8b2-0baf04238897" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472610} {:answer/id #uuid "8c490ab2-ec7b-5dee-94e0-ca23a50fdead" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472611}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186472611} :answer-field/id #uuid "27d756e8-4693-5c8d-a097-a9d17ac33b68" :answer-field/key "A" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473700} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "360e1f52-5cdb-5c5e-9a6d-33c968fdb021" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472612} {:answer/id #uuid "cd099e05-d512-5614-a6fc-51d408232f9d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472613}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186472613} :answer-field/id #uuid "3642312c-08a2-5f05-bb3f-1054acc8e9f4" :answer-field/key "B" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473701} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e87742a-dcd6-5298-bb30-ef2ace74838c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472614} {:answer/id #uuid "6e8e3db4-35ea-53de-88a3-45ed4615b36f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472615}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186472614} :answer-field/id #uuid "924222e4-fc3d-551f-a6c3-451ea17542f0" :answer-field/key "C" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473702}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "3d92198e-4ce7-5520-a0eb-698c6d6eae5d" :question/math-academy-id "q-129231" :question/problem "Which of the following augmented matrices are **not** in row echelon form?\n\n$$\nA=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 7 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right],\\,B=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}5 & 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 1\\end{array}\\right],\\,C=\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}1 & -5 & 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that an augmented matrix is in row echelon form if its coefficient matrix satisfies the following conditions:\n\n- All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the *bottom* of the matrix.\n- Each leading entry of a row is in a column *to the right* of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is not in row echelon form since the second row contains only zeros and it is not at the bottom of the matrix (condition I is violated).\n\n$$\nA=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 7 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ is not in row echelon form since ${b}_{33}\\ne 0$ (condition II is violated).\n\n$$\nB=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}5 & 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 1\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nC=\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}1 & -5 & 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $A$ and $B$ are **not** in row echelon form."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405146 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aeca3672-af73-5de4-ae92-8d2b7267905b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473302} {:answer/id #uuid "3762310e-4280-5383-a623-be69110b6dd6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473303}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186473302} :answer-field/id #uuid "7b242a5e-e0c2-5c98-9faf-9932a432bab4" :answer-field/key "A" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474046} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c468a92d-1de4-54b3-98e3-28167311714f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473304} {:answer/id #uuid "cc55be58-e4c5-5d28-bde2-dd07f224de99" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473305}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186473305} :answer-field/id #uuid "aa9139c6-224d-5848-a9fd-c41516bf7428" :answer-field/key "B" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474047} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "61bba97e-fa99-5844-b1d0-4a1ac0911bd8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473306} {:answer/id #uuid "27aa4326-84a9-502a-8ac6-38a05b1d7790" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473307}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186473306} :answer-field/id #uuid "17d4295d-6d7f-5bde-a6ed-7e5d41c2a614" :answer-field/key "C" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474048}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "bbb2727c-01c4-5345-9e38-1d38c7fb43da" :question/math-academy-id "q-72575" :question/problem "Which of the following augmented matrices have coefficient matrices that are **not** in row echelon form? Treat the final column of each augmented matrix as its constants column.\n\n$$\nA=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 4\\end{array}\\right],\\,B=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}0 & 0 & 4 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 5 & 5\\end{array}\\right],\\,C=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccccc|c}2 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 & 0 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -3 & 1\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A coefficient matrix, obtained by omitting the final column of its augmented matrix, is in row echelon form if it satisfies the following conditions:\n\n- All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the *bottom* of the matrix.\n- Each leading entry of a row is in a column *to the right* of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The coefficient matrix of $A$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nA=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 4\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n- The coefficient matrix of $B$ is not in row echelon form since the leading entries of its first two rows are in columns $3$ and $2,$ respectively (condition II is violated).\n\n$$\nB=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}0 & 0 & 4 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 5 & 5\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n- The coefficient matrix of $C$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nC=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccccc|c}2 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 & 0 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -3 & 1\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $B$ has a coefficient matrix that is **not** in row echelon form."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186413825 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2ff7ff1b-7d10-5900-8b02-8d8762f4648a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472604} {:answer/id #uuid "2a735909-2afd-58c0-8065-6f9b0fda657e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472605}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186472604} :answer-field/id #uuid "f09fe1a5-baa2-5973-acbf-a84cc0ff0a30" :answer-field/key "A" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473697} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9738a799-c696-51e8-87a0-1ab427da9e38" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472606} {:answer/id #uuid "af5402ff-243c-585f-b25c-a8687187c616" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472607}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186472607} :answer-field/id #uuid "1021401d-9baa-5256-9d91-aea06ee1499d" :answer-field/key "B" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473698} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b14007f-a781-5311-9863-6ad6959abeb4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472608} {:answer/id #uuid "d335439c-9eef-5cb8-852d-d00750680628" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472609}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186472609} :answer-field/id #uuid "05c9c089-5c63-5c77-b946-3743f2d68ce2" :answer-field/key "C" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473699}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "a0f43991-a609-584a-a820-e263b283da38" :question/math-academy-id "q-129230" :question/problem "Which of the following augmented matrices are in row echelon form?\n\n$$\nA=\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}-5 & 0 & 8 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & -5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -1\\end{array}\\right],\\,B=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}4 & 0 & 6 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2\\end{array}\\right],\\,C=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}0 & -9 & 0 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that an augmented matrix is in row echelon form if its coefficient matrix satisfies the following conditions:\n\n- All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the bottom of the matrix.\n- Each leading entry of a row is in a column to the right of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is not in row echelon form since ${a}_{33}\\ne 0$ (condition II is violated).\n\n$$\nA=\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}-5 & 0 & 8 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & -5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -1\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nB=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}4 & 0 & 6 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nC=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}0 & -9 & 0 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $B$ and $C$ are in row echelon form."}] :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Augmented Matrices in Row Echelon Form"} :step/id #uuid "9da7e60b-1218-59ef-a17a-68019b1df9c5" :step/math-academy-id 17176 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129941}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129940 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129114 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128926 :question/id #uuid "b6e4983b-c695-5944-9637-6d7547dae849" :question/math-academy-id "e-4688" :question/problem "Which of the following matrices are in row echelon form?\n\n![](images/56/564d16a59313514424d24b8c247d8a3516bfa32188292d2cbc7fee7faf2f5744.svg)" :question/worked-solution "Remember that a matrix is in row echelon form if it satisfies the following conditions:\n\n- All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the *bottom* of the matrix.\n\n- Each leading entry of a row is in a column *to the right* of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is not in row echelon form since the second row contains only zeros and it is not at the bottom of the matrix (condition I is violated).\n![](images/53/53977f4d27cf659f7d595afc4422b0c3009218fe836615eba5faf8a854124c6b.svg)\n\n- The matrix $B$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n![](images/40/40fea7849f3603441671253bb7bc96e56be9bab6a8ddcbc94320238a0e3f529a.svg)\n\n- The matrix $C$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n![](images/08/08ed315816def9b28fb3918a2dd103a5008815fc6a07507b64c5c20572b1c88f.svg)"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2d390841-351e-54f5-ad19-90b6ebae5799" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129773 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "836635cc-25da-5e83-aec4-49f375758900" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459957} {:answer/id #uuid "54eea2b5-b542-5880-be19-6f511782168a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459958}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186459957} :answer-field/id #uuid "04197247-7f0f-56bf-a021-b95053e007e5" :answer-field/key "A" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460845} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "29bb0349-8228-5739-b584-2b4184c57825" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459959} {:answer/id #uuid "213dd0db-1f16-57b8-a75a-94405f576b31" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459960}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186459960} :answer-field/id #uuid "c1992ae7-8a06-5253-8bae-a159ecd12de1" :answer-field/key "B" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460846} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "93932082-4e2a-5d11-9338-3badee54015f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459961} {:answer/id #uuid "3337fae3-8c3b-5ced-a2fe-a0e0b650426e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459962}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186459962} :answer-field/id #uuid "da567c2d-7ca3-5ce0-9d1f-676b0894d8d6" :answer-field/key "C" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460847}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "181e77e0-d595-5539-baef-b4986d4c678b" :question/math-academy-id "q-42024" :question/problem "Which of the following matrices are in row echelon form?\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 5 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 4\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 3 & 6 & 12 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 3 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 5 & 8 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that a matrix is in row echelon form if it satisfies the following conditions:\n\n- All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the *bottom* of the matrix.\n- Each leading entry of a row is in a column *to the right* of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is not in row echelon form since the second row contains only zeros and it is not at the bottom of the matrix (condition I is violated).\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 5 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 3 & 6 & 12 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 3 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 5 & 8 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $B$ and $C$ are in row echelon form."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129778 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b3496ac3-8437-5e13-847a-9b80a3c3fb91" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ and $C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128150} {:answer/id #uuid "b5f43b8e-4ecc-5971-b43f-437aad51b4d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128151} {:answer/id #uuid "034a1eb6-4a74-5fca-831a-b2bb6a34a1bd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$B$ and $C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128152} {:answer/id #uuid "081a0215-3eb3-5aa3-82ad-22c32b803f03" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$B$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128153} {:answer/id #uuid "30e6f031-8d50-57de-b491-2b8b783102ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ and $B$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128154}] :answer-field/id #uuid "c1a50c50-2b60-57e8-b02f-bbbfaf5e7c4c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128149}] :question/id #uuid "d19d6145-1fb1-5d51-b074-044e9b77aefd" :question/math-academy-id "q-42369" :question/problem "Which of the following matrices are **not** in row echelon form?\n\n$A = \\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}, B = \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 1 & 0 & -4 & 9 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 2 & 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 7 & 14\\end{bmatrix}, C = \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262985 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b0c9e6d8-7ba8-5f97-bf70-9b61b4ba882c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/