8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413816}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186413814} :answer-field/id #uuid "9abb4bdb-6a2c-505b-9dc2-250a89af5226" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413820}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "43229055-b652-5005-bf91-54dcfc3e2941" :question/math-academy-id "q-129206" :question/problem "What is the sum of the leading entries of the $1$st, $3$rd, and $4$th rows in the matrix $A,$ given below?\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 0 & -6 \\\\ 4 & 1 & 4 & -9 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -3 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The first non-zero entry of each row (from left to right) is the leading entry. \n\nTherefore, the leading entries of the $1$st, $3$rd, and $4$th rows of $A$ are $-6$, $4$, and $1$, respectively.\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 0 & -6 \\\\ 4 & 1 & 4 & -9 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -3 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSo, the answer is $-6+4+1=-1.$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Leading Entries of a Matrix"} :step/id #uuid "f062c6b3-17e0-57cb-a070-e9edcc0af6c8" :step/math-academy-id 23025 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186130041}}] :activity/title "Row Echelon Form" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186129395}] :db/id #edb/ref 17592186048980 :topic/difficulty 0.4269222604871827 :topic/id #uuid "d0f342d9-c70c-537f-9e04-f3b0beaf9c01" :topic/knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129113 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128925 :question/id #uuid "674e7733-7a8e-5804-a867-82c74c583dcc" :question/math-academy-id "e-4687" :question/problem "Which of the following augmented matrices are in row echelon form?\n![](images/27/2701e789f5d3f6fc48fda87706add41ccb59c92d5bae4a76e84ac1abfdce6f07.svg)" :question/worked-solution "Remember that an augmented matrix is in row echelon form if its coefficient matrix satisfies the following conditions:\n\n- All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the *bottom* of the matrix.\n\n- Each leading entry of a row is in a column *to the right* of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The first matrix is not in row echelon form since $a_{32} \\neq 0$ (condition II is violated).\n![](images/d8/d8725937a4f5f1cfcd36cbe4871a872187df071b54c15d2e29d9b1e3c5f9b731.svg)\n\n- The second matrix is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n![](images/5e/5e3142b1ad4bb219db5d5b144e47fe8d1fa8d1f92c300c6f60fc145cf9424900.svg)\n\n- The third matrix is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n![](images/93/9331fdbede7da49e2dbbc66aac0b3084b1c7acca1ac7e789eded304956a18500.svg)\n\n- The fourth matrix is not in row echelon form since, for example, the leading entry $a_{22}$ lies to the left of the leading entry $a_{13}$ (condition II is violated).\n![](images/76/76e7add6349e0b2fceddf094ac6e3e8cfd0bf1bb43a3fbee0c143b256b81f1c5.svg)"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f5d1d859-0b86-5507-a7bf-3d805a85adf3" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050765}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129771 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b6ac301d-037b-5334-b6d2-fec88197d154" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459951} {:answer/id #uuid "5d1e6f74-c495-5ab5-805c-d983bca1e55c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459952}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186459952} :answer-field/id #uuid "5d0e98e1-9e1f-510d-9dad-15a86b32835a" :answer-field/key "A" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460842} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3b9aa059-0eae-5a76-81c6-21892541d8ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459953} {:answer/id #uuid "0816847a-d539-509b-8356-6a24a780f633" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459954}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186459954} :answer-field/id #uuid "5488b353-c1b4-5e30-83ca-a801084429aa" :answer-field/key "B" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460843} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fd314e1a-8262-5acc-90db-8b8b4a9f82f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459955} {:answer/id #uuid "69a17d39-0448-5a32-8559-ff5820bddc16" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459956}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186459955} :answer-field/id #uuid "eb9e86fc-fb03-5653-aa77-b599aca20dc9" :answer-field/key "C" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460844}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "658776f4-d49a-5e5d-a10c-50a3db34ad1c" :question/math-academy-id "q-42006" :question/problem "Which of the following augmented matrices are in row echelon form?\n\n$$\nA=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}2 & 3 & -7 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 3 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 5\\end{array}\\right],\\,B=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}3 & 1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right],\\,C=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}0 & 0 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 0 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 3 & 2\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that an augmented matrix is in row echelon form if its coefficient matrix satisfies the following conditions:\n\n- All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the bottom of the matrix.\n- Each leading entry of a row is in a column to the right of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nA=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}2 & 3 & -7 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 3 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 5\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nB=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}3 & 1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ is not in row echelon form since ${c}_{22}\\ne 0$ (condition II is violated).\n\n$$\nC=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}0 & 0 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 0 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 3 & 2\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $A$ and $B$ are in row echelon form."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129774 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a12a5bf1-b831-57bc-a289-9b874dd28be1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$B$ and $C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128126} {:answer/id #uuid "0e2e8497-890f-5946-abdd-026c91a6a710" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128127} {:answer/id #uuid "3dd70ee5-9437-5935-856c-7e5b9161b173" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$B$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128128} {:answer/id #uuid "4e86f997-55ba-53d9-bd8d-f236034d4a69" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ and $B$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128129} {:answer/id #uuid "760682b7-9922-52d7-815c-3ae2e12e96e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128130}] :answer-field/id #uuid "84381930-6037-567a-be17-89c5aa7ee6ca" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128125}] :question/id #uuid "532660a0-b7ef-5857-a687-9a224039f8a6" :question/math-academy-id "q-42026" :question/problem "Which of the following augmented matrices are **not** in row echelon form?\n$A = \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 2 & 3\\end{array}\\right], B = \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}2 & 3 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 & 6\\end{array}\\right], C = \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}4 & 0 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262994 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "50c7f862-fb53-52f3-a851-3a1c0dd668c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463742} {:answer/id #uuid "9091f23b-5dc1-5b2b-9de6-80e0b5f2b4c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463743}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186463743} :answer-field/id #uuid "3fe6ae55-4a0c-5261-a839-a0dc70994f94" :answer-field/key "A" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464805} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0925c8c8-8cf1-5109-b122-e948506d2229" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463744} {:answer/id #uuid "87fde758-761e-5f44-8ba8-4f420469834a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463745}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186463745} :answer-field/id #uuid "55a0a25b-6999-500b-b7c6-387f861bd084" :answer-field/key "B" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464806} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ef038684-e790-5680-b0cf-14a5f0791fb3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463746} {:answer/id #uuid "8b0db024-6fc1-5cf1-b6bd-6a6d4a68ed1f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463747}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186463747} :answer-field/id #uuid "c8f73348-51d4-578b-b6eb-9e0e603a1638" :answer-field/key "C" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464807}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "b5479435-9835-502a-bd24-1f955706f0c7" :question/math-academy-id "q-129228" :question/problem "Which of the following augmented matrices are in row echelon form?\n\n$$\nA=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}4 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 3 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -8 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right],\\,B=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}0 & 7 & 0 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right],\\,C=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}0 & 9 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that an augmented matrix is in row echelon form if its coefficient matrix satisfies the following conditions:\n\n- All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the bottom of the matrix.\n- Each leading entry of a row is in a column to the right of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nA=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}4 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 3 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -8 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nB=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}0 & 7 & 0 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nC=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}0 & 9 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nTherefore, $A,$ $B,$ and $C$ are in row echelon form."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262996 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6490d7cb-e49e-5df3-bd24-1fb08e93c1c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463748} {:answer/id #uuid "73f708ba-0076-5c0b-82e1-e919017f5605" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463749}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186463749} :answer-field/id #uuid "2ffde19d-784a-502b-8888-25092d71c5ef" :answer-field/key "A" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464808} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f4750390-d10c-5792-9210-4b235f6e2ce3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463750} {:answer/id #uuid "12e6cef5-b5fe-562c-99cb-370bb6c94767" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463751}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186463751} :answer-field/id #uuid "0a6c5020-e558-5ac4-9259-bee888bb6216" :answer-field/key "B" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464809} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "88129b53-c2d6-50ae-872d-5f80d5c513e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463752} {:answer/id #uuid "8783247a-7590-53f9-8739-7072f4b6b889" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463753}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186463753} :answer-field/id #uuid "90f5dc9c-b2f5-5481-a853-5afc90c32ea7" :answer-field/key "C" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464810}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "0ce5c5ca-b382-5ac8-8df3-b2e87f07de7f" :question/math-academy-id "q-129232" :question/problem "Which of the following augmented matrices are **not** in row echelon form?\n\n$$\nA=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}0 & -4 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 6 & 7\\end{array}\\right],\\,B=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-6 & 3 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 9 & 6 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 5\\end{array}\\right],\\,C=\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}0 & 1 & -4 & 5 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & -7 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 5 & 1\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that an augmented matrix is in row echelon form if its coefficient matrix satisfies the following conditions:\n\nI. All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the *bottom* of the matrix.\n\nII. Each leading entry of a row is in a column *to the right* of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is not in row echelon form since ${a}_{33}\\ne 0$ (condition II is violated).\n\n$$\nA=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}0 & -4 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 6 & 7\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ is not in row echelon form since the third row contains only zeros and it is not at the bottom of the matrix (condition I is violated).\n\n$$\nB=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-6 & 3 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 9 & 6 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 5\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ is not in row echelon form since ${c}_{33}\\ne 0$ (condition II is violated).\n\n$$\nC=\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}0 & 1 & -4 & 5 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & -7 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 5 & 1\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nTherefore, $A,$ $B,$ and $C$ are **not** in row echelon form."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262997 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f2be017f-5e49-5ecf-9256-9026e1e49309" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463754} {:answer/id #uuid "64657d11-388e-5eea-8953-1183ad80b2a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463755}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186463755} :answer-field/id #uuid "7df1ad99-8fc0-5931-8c43-c2f5f1f4ae55" :answer-field/key "A" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464811} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "183285c5-ecf3-5b1b-a709-43802b2d5542" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value 