ix $A$ is not in row echelon form since the first row contains only zeros and it is not at the bottom of the matrix (condition I is violated).\n\n$$\nA=\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0 & 9 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 4 & 6\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nB=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}9 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nC=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 4\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $A$ is **not** in row echelon form."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326923 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "82ceb6ee-967f-51f6-9562-a946e9616bd0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467488} {:answer/id #uuid "5a978d2b-7bde-5c45-a243-0e4e0a33fde7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467489}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186467488} :answer-field/id #uuid "f80dcb05-a2c2-516d-80fe-1ab0eed4e12b" :answer-field/key "A" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468465} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5b08f801-3599-510d-8753-6582f23b7efe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467490} {:answer/id #uuid "62d0a2f4-51a8-5771-9041-0b5950520f2f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467491}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186467490} :answer-field/id #uuid "9d4a18d9-f146-57c1-98ce-7671782922ed" :answer-field/key "B" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468466} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a7ed2b63-95a4-56b7-afb2-010d21ef08ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467492} {:answer/id #uuid "158e4809-5e64-50a5-af3e-ca976103a4d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467493}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186467493} :answer-field/id #uuid "1bbb80cd-ffa5-5028-b638-d29609a12eae" :answer-field/key "C" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468467}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "324c0e93-0bc4-5958-ba8a-b87ad1b81b6a" :question/math-academy-id "q-42028" :question/problem "Which of the following augmented matrices have coefficient matrices in row echelon form? Treat the final column of each augmented matrix as its constants column.\n\n$$\nA=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}2 & 0 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 & 4\\end{array}\\right],\\,\\,B=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}0 & 0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 11\\end{array}\\right],\\,\\,C=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}2 & 4 & 6 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 5\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that an augmented matrix is in row echelon form if its coefficient matrix satisfies the following conditions:\n\n- All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the bottom of the matrix.\n- Each leading entry of a row is in a column to the right of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is not in row echelon form since ${a}_{32}\\ne 0$ (condition II is violated). \n\n$$\nA=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}2 & 0 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 & 4\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ is not in row echelon form since the first row contains only zeros and it is not at the bottom of the matrix (condition I is violated).\n\n$$\nB=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}0 & 0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 11\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nC=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}2 & 4 & 6 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 5\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $C$ is in row echelon form."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186341835 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7311cb50-f585-5f8b-8c7c-43ea3935ca30" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467950} {:answer/id #uuid "5df8e8f3-9308-5944-af31-4d14c71a9d43" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467951}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186467950} :answer-field/id #uuid "00781771-aeb9-5835-884e-fa3c06c40e7e" :answer-field/key "A" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468696} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b1ee2b9e-ef1d-59cf-bd65-2b7d6a2bf08f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467952} {:answer/id #uuid "d81beee0-f7cd-5ee1-a153-c2609ec12ad8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467953}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186467953} :answer-field/id #uuid "625436a2-9099-57c0-a144-3cefd737c380" :answer-field/key "B" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468697} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a341d39f-fed1-52da-a5bf-5551842652b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467954} {:answer/id #uuid "5061ada4-2851-5b12-9dcc-a52396a7b645" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467955}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186467955} :answer-field/id #uuid "4691ceca-21a9-5d3f-be55-1f587cc36770" :answer-field/key "C" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468698}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "4f7d9000-6b1e-59bb-84e6-86f972afc228" :question/math-academy-id "q-72570" :question/problem "Which of the following augmented matrices are in row echelon form?\n\n$$\nA=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 9 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 & 3\\end{array}\\right],\\,\\,B=\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}0 & 2 & 0 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 11 & 1\\end{array}\\right],\\,\\,C=\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}7 & 6 & 6 & 8 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 6 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 4 & 6\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that an augmented matrix is in row echelon form if its coefficient matrix satisfies the following conditions:\n\n- All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the bottom of the matrix.\n- Each leading entry of a row is in a column to the right of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is not in row echelon form since the second row contains only zeros and it is not at the bottom of the matrix (condition I is violated).\n\n$$\nA=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 9 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 & 3\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$  is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nB=\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}0 & 2 & 0 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 11 & 1\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nC=\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}7 & 6 & 6 & 8 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 6 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 4 & 6\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $B$ and $C$ are in row echelon form."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186341837 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "871c0b9a-48a3-59d8-9e1f-f4475d4555bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.t